meta {
  name: Register User
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "password": "SecurePass1"
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
}

docs {
  # POST `/api/auth/register`
  
  Register a new user account.
  
  ---
  
  ## Request
  
  **Method:** `POST`
  **URL:** `/api/auth/register`
  **Content-Type:** `application/json`
  
  ### Request Body
  
  | Field      | Type     | Required | Constraints                                                                                      |
  |------------|----------|----------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
  | `email`    | `string` | Yes      | Must be a valid email address. Automatically lowercased and trimmed.                             |
  | `password` | `string` | Yes      | Min 8 characters, max 128 characters. Must contain at least one uppercase letter and one number. |
  
  ---
  
  ## Responses
  
  ### `200 OK` — User Created Successfully
  
  Returned when the user is registered successfully. The `data` field contains the full user record as inserted into the database.
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "user created successfully",
    "data": {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
      "email": "user@example.com",
      "password": "$2b$10$hashedpasswordstring...",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-02T15:00:00.000Z",
      "updatedAt": null,
      "deletedAt": null
    },
    "meta": {
      "correlationId": "req-abc123-xyz"
    }
  }
  ```
  
  #### Response Shape
  
  | Field                | Type              | Description                                      |
  |----------------------|-------------------|--------------------------------------------------|
  | `success`            | `boolean`         | Always `true` for successful responses.          |
  | `message`            | `string`          | Human-readable status message.                   |
  | `data`               | `object`          | The newly created user record.                   |
  | `data.id`            | `string` (UUID)   | Auto-generated UUID v4 primary key.              |
  | `data.email`         | `string`          | The user's email (lowercased, trimmed).          |
  | `data.password`      | `string`          | The bcrypt-hashed password.                      |
  | `data.createdAt`     | `string` (ISO 8601) | Timestamp of when the record was created.     |
  | `data.updatedAt`     | `string \| null`  | Timestamp of last update, `null` on creation.    |
  | `data.deletedAt`     | `string \| null`  | Soft-delete timestamp, `null` when active.       |
  | `meta`               | `object`          | Request metadata.                                |
  | `meta.correlationId` | `string`          | Correlation ID attached to the request lifecycle.|
  
  ---
  
  ### `400 Bad Request` — Validation Error
  
  Returned when the request body fails Zod schema validation (e.g. missing fields, invalid email, weak password).
  
  ```json
  {
    "status": false,
    "error": {
      "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
      "message": "Request validation failed",
      "details": [
        {
          "field": "email",
          "message": "Must be a valid email"
        },
        {
          "field": "password",
          "message": "Password must be at least 8 characters"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  ```
  
  #### Response Shape
  
  | Field                    | Type       | Description                                             |
  |--------------------------|------------|---------------------------------------------------------|
  | `status`                 | `boolean`  | Always `false` for error responses.                     |
  | `error`                  | `object`   | Error detail container.                                 |
  | `error.code`             | `string`   | Error code: `"VALIDATION_ERROR"`.                       |
  | `error.message`          | `string`   | `"Request validation failed"`.                          |
  | `error.details`          | `array`    | List of individual field validation errors.             |
  | `error.details[].field`  | `string`   | The name of the field that failed validation.           |
  | `error.details[].message`| `string`   | Human-readable description of the validation failure.   |
  
  ---
  
  ### `409 Conflict` — Email Already Exists
  
  Returned when a user with the provided email address already exists in the database.
  
  ```json
  {
    "status": false,
    "error": {
      "code": "CONFLICT",
      "message": "Email already exists"
    }
  }
  ```
  
  #### Response Shape
  
  | Field           | Type      | Description                                    |
  |-----------------|-----------|------------------------------------------------|
  | `status`        | `boolean` | Always `false` for error responses.            |
  | `error`         | `object`  | Error detail container.                        |
  | `error.code`    | `string`  | Error code: `"CONFLICT"`.                      |
  | `error.message` | `string`  | `"Email already exists"`.                      |
  
  ---
  
  ### `500 Internal Server Error` — Unexpected Error
  
  Returned when an unhandled or non-operational error occurs (e.g. database connection failure, user insertion failure).
  
  ```json
  {
    "status": false,
    "error": {
      "code": "INTERNAL_ERROR",
      "message": "An unexpected error occured"
    }
  }
  ```
  
  #### Response Shape
  
  | Field           | Type      | Description                                    |
  |-----------------|-----------|------------------------------------------------|
  | `status`        | `boolean` | Always `false` for error responses.            |
  | `error`         | `object`  | Error detail container.                        |
  | `error.code`    | `string`  | Error code: `"INTERNAL_ERROR"`.                |
  | `error.message` | `string`  | `"An unexpected error occured"`.               |
  
  ---
}
